***********************************************************************
*                    EMC - INSTALLATION GUIDE                         *
***********************************************************************

1. EXTRACT THE ARCHIVE
   Open your terminal and run these commands to extract the files:

   cd ~/Downloads
   tar -xvf EMC_INSTALL_standalone.tar.gz -C ~

2. RUN INSTALLATION
   Start the base installer script:

   ~/EMC_install/EMC_standalone_base_installer.sh 

   The installer guides you through three stages:
   - Step 1 (Preinstall) : Prepare the installation media (ISO/USB).
   - Step 2 (Install)    : System deployment and package installation.
   - Step 3 (Postinstall): Final setup and reboot.

   Use the 'help' command within each menu for further guidance!

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-                      AFTER INSTALLATION ...                         -
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

EMC Commander start instructions:

   1. After reboot, boot the partition where EMC Commander is installed.
   2. After login, start EMC Commander with: startx
   3. Left  click on space in the mainbar in the bottom of your screen will open Mainbar info window.
   4. Click the [EMC app installer] button in the Mainbar info window to install additional software.

The launchers are pre-configured. If an application is missing, you 
will receive a notification at startup. You can install missing apps 
via the 'App Installer' (accessible via the mainbar info window).

Use [ Application setup ] in mainbar info window or file starters to edit configuration files.
- Scroll UP/DOWN on an icon in launchbar to see its tooltip.
- Right-click space in the mainbar to open the setup window.

CONFIGURATION FILES:
- Launchbars & Tooltips: $HOME/.config/polybar/usr/               [Application setup]
- Workspace Icons      : $HOME/.config/i3/usr/config_workspaces   [file starter 4 l]
- Autostart/Commands   : $HOME/.config/i3/usr/config_usercommands [file starter 4 r]

MONITOR CONFIG
-actual resolution     : $HOME/.config/polybar/usr/monitor.ini    dbl-left display module
-resolution templates  : $HOME/.config/polybar/usr/monitor

LOG FILES:
- Installer logs and system reports are stored in: $HOME/.config/polybar/log

See Documentation on github!

